Title: SENIOR WEEK
Author: Priya Shah
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


EXT. HIGH SCHOOL - ESTABLISHING - DAY

Banners: CLASS OF 2026. Last bell energy everywhere.

INT. HALLWAY - DAY

MAYA pins a senior-week schedule. JORDAN watches, skeptical.
MAYA
One perfect week before everything splits.

INT. GUIDANCE OFFICE - DAY

Maya gets financial aid confirmation — coast school real. Jordan fakes a smile.

EXT. ROOFTOP - AFTERNOON

Yearbooks, cider, signatures.
JORDAN
Facetime isn't a friendship.

INT. MAYA'S GARAGE - NIGHT

They build flats for an unauthorized senior play.
MAYA
Something that doesn't fit in a dorm box.

INT. AUDITORIUM - NIGHT

Guerrilla show begins — small audience, big heart.

INT. BACKSTAGE - NIGHT

Principal's footsteps. Jordan kills the lights. Hands find hands.

EXT. LOADING DOCK - NIGHT

Cast escapes laughing. Security flashlight sweeps empty aisles.

INT. PRINCIPAL'S OFFICE - NEXT DAY

Maya and Jordan sit, not sorry. Suspension threatened, then reduced.
PRINCIPAL
You broke three rules. You also gave twelve seniors a memory.

EXT. PARKING LOT - NIGHT

Graduation eve. Hood of Maya's car. Jordan hands her a USB — the show recorded from the sound board.
JORDAN
Same thing if you're paying attention. Perfect or real.
MAYA
Real. Always real.

FADE OUT.


THE END
